-An HTTP server that routes each request by the method and target in its request line.
+﻿An HTTP server that parses each request (request line, headers and any `Content-Length` body) and routes it by method and target.
 
 Run: `node server.js`
 
 Minimum Node.js version: 22
 
 Port: 8080
+
+Routes:
+- `/echo` replies with `<METHOD> <path>` (query string excluded) for any method
+- `/` and `/users/:userId/posts/:postId` respond to `GET`
+
+Malformed requests (bad request line or header, invalid or conflicting `Content-Length`, `Transfer-Encoding`, oversized request line or headers, or a connection closed before the request is complete) get `400 Bad Request`. A body larger than `MAX_BODY_BYTES` gets `413`.
+
+Limits (env vars): `MAX_REQUEST_LINE_BYTES` (8192), `MAX_HEADER_BYTES` (16384), `MAX_BODY_BYTES` (1048576).
